{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And HaShem spoke, etc.</b> The reckoning of the utterance would suggest that only now HaShem begins to speak to him concerning this matter, but that is not so, for HaShem had already spoken many things concerning this as stated in the preceding verses. Rather, the explanation is that the things that had passed from HaShem to Moses until now were matters between Him and Moses alone, not as a mission to Israel — and the discerning reader will find vindicated, in light of what we have explained, the fact that it was nothing but like a king speaking with his servant about matters he wishes to carry out. Therefore there He did not say ״לֵאמֹר״ at all. But here He begins to speak to him words of mission to Israel, and therefore it says <b>and HaShem spoke</b>, etc. — to say the things to Israel as written."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:09:18.245869701Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}